    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a clear emphasis on aggressive baserunning and high-leverage leadoff spots, highlighted by our two strongest plays: **Trea Turner** (67.66) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (67.31). **Trea Turner** is the cornerstone of our lineup against Peralta, benefiting from a slow delivery matchup that projects a high probability for a stolen base, a critical advantage given the league's scarcity. Similarly, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** earns his high score by taking advantage of a soft matchup against Corbin. While his platoon disadvantage (L/L) drags his ceiling down slightly, the elite 4.62 xERA of the opposing starter and the premium leadoff spot provide a high floor for runs and SB potential.\n\nIn terms of mid-tier value, **Kyle Schwarber** (63.03) and **Yordan Alvarez** (62.94) provide essential power, though both must navigate suboptimal platoon splits. **Kazuma Okamoto** (60.37) remains a reliable start today, as he is one of the few hitters in our lineup enjoying a positive SP skill adjustment against a favorable matchup (Rea, 4.53 xERA). The most difficult bench decision involved **Junior Caminero** (58.98); while he missed the official starting cut by a narrow margin, his power profile against Cavalli makes him our primary pinch-hit candidate should the game state require late-inning run production.\n\nWe remain cautious regarding **Gary Sanchez** (40.57) and **Carson Benge** (41.02), both of whom are operating near the bottom of our efficiency floor due to difficult matchups against Sale and S\u00e1nchez respectively. Sale\u2019s 3.01 xERA is a significant hurdle, and **Gary Sanchez** specifically faces a BvP headwind that limits his expectations. We are monitoring all lineups closely for **Christian Yelich** and **Colt Keith**, but with both currently out of their respective starting lineups, our strategy remains fixed on the speed-oriented core of **Trea Turner**, **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, and **Dillon Dingler** to manufacture points in a day where pitching matchups are largely challenging.",
